// The third stratum (negates the second): a filter goes after the atom that binds the last of its variables, and is
// then moved. A filter with no variable, or one an atom never binds, stays where it was written: the executor refuses
// the second (B§7).
place(d, r, f, k) :- in_filter(d, r, f, v), binds(d, r, v, k), !waits(d, r, f, k).
moved(d, r, f) :- place(d, r, f, _).
